Recommends: fonts-noto-color-emoji
Description: local clipboard history and Unicode emoji picker for GNOME Shell
 Super V Ubuntu adds a compact Super+V shell popup with searchable text
 history, pins, local persistence, and a Unicode emoji picker. It uses
 GNOME's Wayland clipboard and virtual keyboard APIs without a daemon.
 Users must enable the extension in their own GNOME session. Desktop
 runtime validation is pending; automated logic and package tests exist.
